@@ -6,6 +6,19 @@ This project follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/). Each release is
 
 ---
 
+## Unreleased
+
+### Fixed
+
+- PR-001 no longer accepts I2C-capable peers' CLK/DO-like pin aliases as SPI proof. The clock/data pair must share one peer with no I2C role on those distinct nets. Unrelated clock/data peers and a single clock/data net remain unresolved.
+- PP-001 recognizes ANODE/CATHODE and explicit pin-function polarity metadata for two-pin gate diodes. Numeric pin numbers alone, conflicting metadata and unknown polarity retain errors.
+
+
+- PP-001 (`audit_power_pin_dc_paths`) no longer reports a pin as AC-coupled when the netlist sources it under stated assumptions, and never clears it silently. A pin that reaches no named rail or connector is re-walked: another component's `power_out` pin counts as a source once that component is itself powered (a least fixed point, so regulators cannot vouch for each other in a loop), and a P-MOSFET is crossed drain↔source only when its gate is a ground net or has a resistor to ground with no competing pull-up (a capacitor, a gate-source clamp diode or an anode-on-gate diode to ground is allowed). Such a pin gets an `info` PP-001 finding whose `assumptions` list names the trusted `power_out` regulation (transitively) and the unproven `|VGS(th)|`/clamp margins. A competing gate pull-up (the divider ratio is reported), a driven gate, a gate on a rail, a floating gate or a diode that can pull the gate up keeps the error and names the unresolved conduction in `unresolved`. An unpowered `power_out` owner, the audited IC's own `power_out`, N-channel FETs, gate-net paths and capacitor-only supplies stay reported.
+- PR-001 (`validate_i2c_bus`) classifies a dual-mode device's SDA/SCL pins as SPI only on positive topology evidence: its chip-select is driven by another component's output/bidirectional/tri-state pin AND other components carry SPI-only pin names (SCK/CLK/SPC on the clock net, MOSI/SDI/DIN/… on the data net). An `info` finding records the evidence. A driven chip-select without that topology leaves the mode unresolved: an `info` finding says so and the missing-pull-up errors stay. Both notes name the evidence components, so they never take a pull-up error's finding identity.
+
+---
+
 ## v2.3.1 — 2026-10-06
 
 **Theme: maintenance — one field-recognition gap from the field, six v2.3.0 follow-ups, two regressions the corpus gate caught before the tag, and three defects a fresh-eyes soak found on a real board. Every change gated over the full corpus; the one output change that is not additive is the MPN re-ranking.**
