 - **Vout estimation**: Feedback divider Vout uses hardcoded Vref guesses (0.6, 0.8, 1.0, 1.22, 1.25V) without a component database
 - **Regulator output_rail**: Switching regulators sometimes show null output_rail when the power net is on the inductor output side
 - **Eagle files**: Not parseable — output 0 components
+
+### PP-001 / PR-001 conservative topology boundaries
+
+PP-001 records `power_out` trust and held-low P-MOSFET threshold/clamp margins
+in explicit `assumptions` (`source_path: assumed`). An info severity does not
+establish conduction or regulation; consumers must require an evidence-backed
+disposition before using such a finding for acceptance. Competing or unknown
+gate paths retain errors. Diode polarity uses A/K, ANODE/CATHODE, or explicit
+`pin_function` metadata on net pins/component pins; numeric pin numbers alone
+never establish orientation. Conflicting or missing polarity and multi-pin
+diodes remain unresolved.
+
+PR-001 requires an actively driven chip-select plus a clock/data pin pair on
+one peer, on distinct nets. Peers with I2C aliases (including composite
+SCL/SPC, SDA/SDI/SDO, I2C_CLK and SDA_DO) or known I2C part roles cannot establish
+SPI. A clock token on one part and a data token on an unrelated part do not
+establish SPI. Ambiguous mode retains I2C missing-pull-up errors.
+
+Run the owned contract regressions with:
+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest skills/kicad/scripts/test_power_and_bus_classification.py -v`.
